 "text": "He sat down opposite the treasury and watched people give. On purpose. Mark twelve. And the setup is the part everyone skips. \"Jesus sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury.\" He sat down. And watched. Deliberately. And many that were rich cast in much. That is in the text too. It is not a lie. They gave a lot. Then a certain poor widow comes and throws in two mites. And Mark actually converts the currency for his readers, which tells you how small it was. Two mites, which make a farthing. And Jesus calls his disciples over. He wants them to see this specifically. \"Verily I say unto you, That this poor widow hath cast more in, than all they which have cast into the treasury.\" More than all of them. Combined. And then he does the maths out loud. \"For all they did cast in of their abundance; but she of her want did cast in all that she had, even all her living.\" All her living. Not a percentage. Everything. He is not measuring the gift. He is measuring what was left afterwards.",
